{"event": "llm_route", "client_s": 4.753, "data": {"request_id": "262f74570c99", "seq": 20, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:08:23.216Z", "t_ms": 4619, "call_site": "synthesize", "agent": "synthesizer", "provider": "gemini-openrouter", "model_id": "google/gemini-3.8-flash", "dimension": "cost", "rationale": "Grounded answer from 1 paper and one worker result; the low-cost model is sufficient.", "features": {"n_tasks": 1, "n_tasks_ok": 1, "n_evidence": 7, "n_papers": 1, "n_web": 0, "n_data": 0, "evidence_tokens_est": 3679, "comparison": false, "statuses": ["done"], "evidence_only": true}, "reasoning_effort": "minimal", "timeout_s": 60.0, "price_checked": "2026-10-27", "decision_id": "b8c77756", "provider_label": "Google Gemini (served through OpenRouter)"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 6.685, "data": {"request_id": "262f74570c99", "seq": 21, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:08:25.155Z", "t_ms": 6558, "delta": "The"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 6.834, "data": {"request_id": "262f74570c99", "seq": 22, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:08:25.304Z", "t_ms": 6707, "delta": " RAPTOR paper builds its retrieval tree from the following components and bottom-up process:\n\n*"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.047, "data": {"request_id": "262f74570c99", "seq": 23, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:08:25.518Z", "t_ms": 6921, "delta": " **Leaf nodes from text chunks:** Tree construction begins by segmenting the retrieval corpus into short, contiguous text chunks of 10"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.206, "data": {"request_id": "262f74570c99", "seq": 24, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:08:25.677Z", "t_ms": 7080, "delta": "0 tokens [C2]. If a sentence exceeds this limit, the whole sentence is shifted to the next chunk rather than split"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.385, "data": {"request_id": "262f74570c99", "seq": 25, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:08:25.855Z", "t_ms": 7259, "delta": " mid-sentence to preserve coherence [C2]. These chunks are embedded using SBERT (`multi-qa-mpnet-base"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.503, "data": {"request_id": "262f74570c99", "seq": 26, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:08:25.975Z", "t_ms": 7378, "delta": "-cos-v1`), forming the leaf nodes of the tree [C2].\n* **Higher-level nodes"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.764, "data": {"request_id": "262f74570c99", "seq": 27, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:08:26.208Z", "t_ms": 7611, "delta": " from clustering and summarization:** To form higher layers, the nodes are clustered using Gaussian Mixture Models (GMMs) coupled"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.925, "data": {"request_id": "262f74570c99", "seq": 28, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:08:26.393Z", "t_ms": 7796, "delta": " with UMAP for dimensionality reduction, which allows soft clustering across multiple topics [C2, C3]. A language model (specifically"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.086, "data": {"request_id": "262f74570c99", "seq": 29, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:08:26.558Z", "t_ms": 7961, "delta": " `gpt-3.5-turbo`) then summarizes each cluster of grouped texts [C2, C4].\n"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.305, "data": {"request_id": "262f74570c99", "seq": 30, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:08:26.777Z", "t_ms": 8180, "delta": "* **Recursive tree structure:** The resulting summary texts are re-embedded, clustered, and summarized recursively until further clustering becomes infeasible,"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.529, "data": {"request_id": "262f74570c99", "seq": 31, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:08:26.999Z", "t_ms": 8402, "delta": " yielding a structured, multi-layered tree of summaries at varying levels of abstraction [C1, C2]."}}
